WEBVTT

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.190
Even knowing I can come back 
to life, that's scary...

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:30.970
There.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.160
How many times have I fallen now?

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.250
I don't need my eyes anymore, anyway.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.280
I can focus better this way.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.100
This is Yotsuya Yuusuke-kun, 
our new student.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.790
I-I just moved here from Kumamoto.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.270
M-My name's Y-Yotsuya Y-Yuusuke.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.770
Time to pick your groups 
for the field trip.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.160
Divide up into groups of six friends each.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.780
C'mon, someone take Yotsuya in.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.750
Hey, you guys only have five.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.000
Aw, man!

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.850
Seriously?

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.550
I'm going to go raise my rank.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.210
Later.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.540
I bet you designed this to 
be unclimbable, didn't you?

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:03.950
But I just climbed it, Master!

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:48.780
Damn it. This map only gives 
me the top-down view.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.590
Light? Is that a log point?

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:09.890
You served my family well for these 
ten years and three months.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.940
Warrior Bihmsberg...

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:20.510
I will send those three soldiers from Deokk

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:25.040
to join you within the coming
days, so you can cut them apart.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.810
Make no mistake about that!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.130
He's here...

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.050
Wow, this is good.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.610
Aw...

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.530
Bihmsberg-san...

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.790
One...

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:44.770
Two, and...

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:45.720
Three!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.030
<i>This happened because I 
joined up with Kahvel-san.</i>

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:05.100
<i>But now...</i>

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.690
This is the second time I've 
pushed a carriage with you.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.790
Yeah, I guess so.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:15.520
<i>I didn't know him long, 
but he was my comrade in arms.</i>

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:14.500
It won't be much longer. Let's keep it up!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.520
Right!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.660
<i>Comrade in arms...</i>

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.440
<i>I didn't even get to see 
his face as he died.</i>

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.140
Thank you for everything.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.790
<i>I guess I'm just always going to be...</i>

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.140
Goodbye.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.460
<i>...a stranger to everyone.</i>

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.720
God, these vampire bats are 
getting on my nerves!

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.310
Bear with it!

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.580
I'll take pleasure in cutting you up.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.390
Look! On his arm!

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:48.060
I see. So we have to get the key...

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.210
if we want to get out of here!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.150
Out of the four of you...

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.500
you definitely have the most talent.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:04.550
Thanks! Until just recently, 
I spent two years playing a sport

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:07.370
where I hit really small 
targets with a stick!

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:09.090
Why did you stop?

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.010
You should continue playing that sport!

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:19.770
I really thought you could 
make the top eight.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:21.790
Out after the first round...

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:25.620
Too bad. Were you nervous because 
it's your last tournament?

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:26.680
No...

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:30.110
<i>My weakness as a Wizard is 
my low physical strength.</i>

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:34.960
<i>The stats of this world carried 
over into the real world.</i>

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.900
<i>All because of that half-faced freak...</i>

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.450
I'm so disappointed...

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:45.490
I will. You can bet on it.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:46.370
In high school—

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:05.470
Kahvel-san!

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.350
<i>No way...</i>

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.830
<i>Kahvel-san is dead?</i>

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:16.970
What?! Wait, no, no, no!

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.340
I can't handle him!

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:39.190
He stopped?

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.560
When you reach rank 10,

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.480
time stops for everyone but you 
and the Master, and then...

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.670
Rank 10... I'm changing jobs?

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.800
Congratula.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.140
Your job rank has reached 10.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.810
It's time to spin the 
wheel for the job roul.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.830
You were a wizard—

00:09:58.830 --> 00:09:59.790
You're too late!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.780
A few seconds... A few seconds earlier, 
and I could've saved Kahvel-san!

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:04.750
Now...

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:11.110
Until he hits the play button 
and time starts moving again...

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.890
It's only for a few seconds...

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:15.760
But if there's an enemy near you...

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.510
Bam!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.430
...you have a chance...

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.250
to jump into close range!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.670
Shindou Iu, Warrior (Sword).

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:31.020
Die!

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:36.030
m 0 0 l 258 0 l 258 200 l 0 200

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:36.030
<b>[Rank Up Bonus]</b>

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:36.030
►Occurs simultaneously with a job change.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:39.870
<i>It's so hard!</i>

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.120
Oh, my left arm's healed!

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.950
Damn these bats!

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.870
My hat, my hat...

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:24.870
<b>Wizard Clothes (Top)</b>

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:24.870
<b>Wizard Hat</b>

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:24.870
<b>Wizard Staff (Wind)</b>

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:27.230
And my shield.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:31.750
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.200
<i>Did Kahvel-san give him that wound?</i>

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:37.580
<i>My sword didn't even leave a mark.</i>

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:42.760
Which means cutting locations that will 
cause instant death or a fatal wound.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.930
Do you know where those are?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.170
Uh... the neck?

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:48.860
You're partially right.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:52.440
But the neck is usually protected by armor.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.340
Your best bet is always...

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:55.270
the heart.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.060
Huh? But...

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.200
Yes, the chest appears to be protected 
by both armor and bones,

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.210
but so long as they aren't 
in full plate armor,

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.180
there are usually seams 
between armor pieces.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.310
From above, you would enter here...

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.540
and from below, you would enter here.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.680
The only way to make up the difference 
in strength between men and women

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:16.710
is with techniques like these...

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.230
With sword art.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.170
<i>Right... His ribs are there.</i>

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.090
<i>And if his heart is in the 
same place as a human's...</i>

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.190
<i>It's worth a try!</i>

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:36.980
Ow!

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.930
<i>I think it's getting a 
little brighter in here.</i>

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:08.880
<i>I'm almost there!</i>

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:14.640
<i>I consider all life to 
be not equal, but fair.</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:15.100
Hideout

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.000
A bear!

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.600
<i>That means the value of each life 
can be expressed as a score,</i>

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:36.660
<i>making it possible to rank them.</i>

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.560
<i>Why was I born?</i>

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.160
<i>Why was I chosen to be a player?</i>

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.400
<i>Why am I...</i>

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.380
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:52.350
Shindou-san's amazing.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.570
So I learned that my friends 
are my strength.

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:58.930
And that I'm responsible for 
changing my own world...

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.440
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.030
I want to help everyone now, 
while I'm healthy...

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.250
And you know...

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.180
if I abandoned a child...

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:13.320
there'd be no point anymore.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:14.910
<i>And you...</i>

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.640
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:35.760
<i>What's my reason for existing? 
The reason I was chosen as a player?</i>

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.190
<i>Our current party lineup...</i>

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.330
<i>The job roulette results seem 
like they're being manipulated.</i>

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:48.090
<i>One thing I could consider 
as a possible answer...</i>

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:51.410
<i>is that I'm in the role of the leader.</i>

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:53.540
<i>I'll do my part.</i>

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:54.880
<i>I have to.</i>

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:59.940
<i>At the very least, given our 
current combat abilities...</i>

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:04.300
<i>I'm the strongest of us!</i>

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.180
Yotsuya-kun?!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.370
Yotsuya-san!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.400
Oh... Yotsuya-kun.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.960
You're way late.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:24.360
Y-Yeah... s-so I see...

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.150
Yotsuya-san!

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.990
Kahvel-san is... Kahvel-san is...

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.980
She's down there!

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.170
Can you hel—

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:45.840
I'm saying the safety of each one of us, 
individually, is irrelevant to the quest.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:48.550
<i>He'll save Kahvel-san, though.</i>

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.060
<i>Oh, good! Yotsuya-kun finally gets it!</i>

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:06.150
Oh, Kahvel-san! Thank goodness!

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.060
I'm... alive?

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:11.240
Ow!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.470
My wound...

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.470
The hero healed it.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.180
He consumed blood from monsters in the cave

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.220
in his determination to heal you.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:35.320
He emptied those containers 
healing you over and over.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:39.840
As soon as he finished, 
he fell dead asleep.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.140
He's been like that ever since.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:50.760
<i>I didn't know heroes' eyes rolled back 
into their heads when they slept.</i>

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.320
<i>And he's stretched out 
straight as an arrow.</i>

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.380
I'll go call the others.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.220
All right.

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.710
Why did you do that?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.070
It just... happened.

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.290
Wait, did someone already 
have a claim on him?

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.610
Oh, no, no!

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:22.630
I thought not.

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:26.560
He reminds me of me somehow.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.860
He does? But how...

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.980
<i>Oh. 'Cause they're both weird.</i>

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.640
The way he's struggling.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.650
He's trying to find out who he is,

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.390
how much he's capable of,

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.380
how far he has to go and what he has to do

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:43.660
before he can die with the pride of 
knowing his life meant something.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:48.080
In my country, we use a league 
system to rank knights.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.840
There are 3,000 participants,

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.720
and the top 100 can become knights.

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.550
I ranked 70th.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:55.970
You were 70th out of 3,000?

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:57.350
That's impressive!

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:03.140
My father ranked 2nd, 
my older brother ranked 8th,

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.030
and my younger brother ranked 15th.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.040
I'm just average, really.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.080
No matter how hard I try, 
I can't make up the difference.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:14.780
Is that one of your reasons 
for leading this expedition?

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.760
Possibly, but the main reason...

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.400
was so I could slice up flesh.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:20.450
<i>She never breaks character!</i>

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.670
If I have any chance of turning it around,

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:25.370
it would be in a real battle.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:30.780
My father told me, "One real battle 
is worth 10,000 practice swings."

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:34.790
Yes, what he meant was, 
"Slice up living flesh."

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.960
<i>There it is again!</i>

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:40.500
How far have they gone ahead?

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:44.450
They took the long way by going over the 
mountain, so we should catch up quickly.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:48.450
We have about seven days 
and ten hours left...

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.240
Can we make it?

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.020
I'm not sure.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.560
When's he going to wake up?

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.630
I had it all wrong!

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.510
Whoa! You scared me!

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:03.360
What?!

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:04.780
What just happened?

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:10.400
Wait, seriously, what's wrong?

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:11.700
The "goods"...

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:14.320
What do you think "the goods" are?

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:17.210
The goods? Like... merchandise?

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:20.890
Right. Something that you can sell, 
or that people might want...

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.880
Things worth transporting long distances.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:27.050
And... what do you think 
"village chief" means?

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:31.200
Village chief? Why? 
You mean the one from that other quest?

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.720
The leader of a village, right?

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:37.060
Right, the third quest was to fulfill 
the village chief's request.

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:41.280
But no specific village or 
person was actually named.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.900
So what are you saying?

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:50.110
What if our third quest could've referred to 
<i>any</i> request by <i>any</i> leader of <i>any</i> village?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.590
Shindou-san, what was the first quest?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.130
<b><<Defeat 1 goblin>></b>

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:55.120
To defeat one goblin.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.540
The goblins we always see

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.380
are a type called meri goblins that 
are native to this continent,

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:05.080
but I'm betting there are other 
types of goblins in this world.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:07.310
Well, sure...

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:10.860
So maybe it didn't matter what 
type of goblin you defeated.

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:12.390
What was second?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.150
<b><<Find 2 settlements>></b>

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.150
To find two settlements.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:19.270
I bet it didn't matter which 
settlements you found.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.970
Well, no specific ones were named...

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:24.240
And we cleared it based on that assumption.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:24.940
Yeah.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:27.300
There you go. What I'm saying is,

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:29.610
anything that can be classified as "goods"

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:33.830
is likely to count toward the 
completion of our quest.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.290
So?

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:38.240
That brings us back to what's 
meant by "the goods."

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:42.420
If you define it that way, there's a good 
chance it's not the condemned convicts.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.130
Huh?

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:46.210
Because there's no one in Radodorbo 
waiting to accept them,

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:48.380
and no advance notice of 
any exchange to be made.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.470
What?! You mean we've...

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:53.660
been on a fool's errand all this time?

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:56.670
But...

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.310
But hang on a second, Yotsuya-kun!

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:03.730
Are you... Are you going to abandon 
the three convicts this time, too?

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:05.690
One of them is a child!

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:09.420
Unlike us, if they die, they'll die for real!

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:11.330
Well, I mean...

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:15.600
There's still a chance the condemned 
convicts could be the "goods,"

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:20.350
so it doesn't eliminate the chance that we 
could fail the quest if we abandon them.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:22.500
What should we do?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.090
Okay. Let's split up.

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:31.730
<i>Wait... What is this?</i>

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:35.020
<i>Why do I feel like I've been dumped 
by a guy I didn't ask out?</i>

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:40.020
<b>The Warrior of Light and the Stranger of Darkness</b>

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:11.900
Get Through the Dungeon!

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:11.910
<b>Get Through the Dungeon!</b>

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:15.150
What's this?

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:15.740
<b>Door to

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:18.190
Ooh! Is Tsubasa-kyun up ahead?!

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:19.180
I'll go check it ou—

